* your user feedback summary for a user testing your Project 1 (caption generation and rating app)

Key Learnings:
- Users value both simplicity and engagement differently
- Voting interaction style (scroll vs flashcards) impacted usability and speed of interaction
- Clear visibility for votes, generated content, and content updates is important for user understanding

Surprises:
- Some users preferred scrolling for flexibility, while others found it inefficient
- The same design choice (plain layout, repeated images) was interpreted both positively and negatively
- Content being both repetitive and unpredictably reordered caused confusion rather than variety

Patterns Across Users:
- Difficulty with voting interaction while scrolling
- Repetition of content reduced engagement over time
- Desire for more feedback such as vote tracking and generated content results
- Inconsistent or unclear content updates such as order changes and recycled memes caused confusion

Planned Improvements:
- Add a flashcard style voting mode as an alternative to scrolling
- Improve content consistency such as reduce repetition and avoid unexpected reordering
- Add voting history and allow users to review past upvotes/downvotes
- Improve caption generation flow by adding generated content directly to the feed or providing confirmation
- Add progress indicator or number of remaining memes
- Add basic analytics like percentage of votes or top memes

Summary of Changes After Feedback: 

1 Enhanced Account/ Auth UI
Added clear account section with welcome message (username) and logout -> improves clarity of login state

2 Enhanced UI Consistency & Engagement
Redesigned layout with consistent card styling and spacing -> addresses feedback that the app felt plain and empty

3 Enhanced Voting Interaction UI
Enlarged and centered vote buttons -> reduces cursor accuracy issues and supports faster voting

4 Added Flashcard/ Feed Mode Toggle
Introduced flashcard mode (one by one, faster voting) and feed mode (scrollable, revisit votes) -> addresses different user preferences for interaction 

5 Added Voting Progress Indicator
Displayed voted and remaining memes with a progress bar -> resolves uncertainty about how many memes are left 

6 Added Vote History Feature
Showed past votes with totals (votes, upvotes, downvotes) -> improves visibility of user activity, gives the user more control

7 Enhanced Content Loading & Consistency
Implemented step by step loading with “Load More” button -> reduces repetition and prevents random reordering 

8 Enhanced Caption Generation Feedback
Added confirmation messages and displays generated captions -> clarifies post generation flow

9 Enhanced Navigation & Usability
Added mode toggle, vote history access, and scroll controls -> improves overall navigation and user flow


